## Decide whether the task needs a data dashboard

Use a monitoring overview for a question people return to and data that can be kept up to date. Give occasional readers enough context to understand the measures. A fixed report can be a better fit for a one-off explanation or a result that needs substantial interpretation. Review the need again when the household, sources or task changes. This adapts the [GOV.UK dashboard guidance](https://brand.design-system.service.gov.uk/data/dashboards/).

| Household need | Suitable presentation | Essential context |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Repeatedly check grid import during a selected period | A small set of indicators, an interval chart and its values | Period, unit, source, missing intervals and the difference between a partial sum and a complete total |
| Compare a few room observations at a stated time | A text-first report or table | Per-room observation time, source, coverage and any reason to exclude an old value |
| Explain a detailed change or investigate a fault | A focused history view or written report | Evidence, comparison conditions and an explanation that the overview cannot supply |

The [data guidance](../styles/brand-data.html) connects these choices to charts, dashboards and maps. **BG-DAT-01** starts with the question, **BG-DAT-03** supplies measure, period and source, and **BG-DAT-07** provides a usable alternative. [BG-COL-02](../styles/brand-colour.html#bg-col-02) keeps identity, status and data colours separate; [BG-COL-07](../styles/brand-colour.html#bg-col-07) preserves meaningful chart identities and scales.

## A monitoring overview with matching chart data

This example answers one question about grid import. The indicators, column chart and table use the same six hourly intervals. One interval is missing, so the page states a partial sum and qualifies the largest recorded value. A local link leads to the source and coverage explanation; it does not open a pretend device control.

The chart is a static SVG reference, with opaque square columns, a zero baseline and the shared grid-import colour. It applies the documented chart roles but does not run the native Energy adapter. Use the [maintained chart specification and working renderer examples](../components/charts.html) for the production integration and its supported scope. All values here are invented.

