## A text-first report when coverage is incomplete

This second example keeps every room visible while distinguishing observations inside the review window, an older observation and a room with no configured sensor. It uses a reading list because the immediate task does not need another chart. The source details explain why a household-wide average is absent.

Its five-minute window is an explicit example decision. A real installation needs an appropriate observation contract for each source; a theme cannot infer freshness from colour or a generic last-changed timestamp. See [entity state, confidence and freshness](../home-assistant/entity-state.html) when defining that contract.

